[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Machine Learning and Vector Search (KNN) in Elasticsearch"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Vector search enables you to find similar items based on their semantic meaning rather than exact keyword matches. By leveraging Machine Learning models to generate vector embeddings, Elasticsearch allows you to perform k-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) searches efficiently at scale."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 1: Define an Index Mapping with Dense Vectors"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To store and query vector embeddings in Elasticsearch, you must define an index mapping with a field of type "dense_vector". You specify the dimensionality of the vectors and the similarity metric (such as "cosine" or "l2_norm")."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"PUT /product_catalog
{
  "mappings": {
    "properties": {
      "product_id": { "type": "keyword" },
      "product_name": { "type": "text" },
      "product_vector": {
        "type": "dense_vector",
        "dims": 3,
        "index": true,
        "similarity": "cosine"
      }
    }
  }
}"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 2: Ingest Data with Vector Embeddings"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once your index is created, you can index documents containing both traditional textual data and numerical vector arrays generated by your ML model."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"POST /product_catalog/_doc/1
{
  "product_id": "P001",
  "product_name": "Ergonomic Office Chair",
  "product_vector": [0.12, 0.88, 0.45]
}

POST /product_catalog/_doc/2
{
  "product_id": "P002",
  "product_name": "Gaming Chair",
  "product_vector": [0.15, 0.85, 0.50]
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 3: Execute a KNN Search Query"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can perform approximate k-Nearest Neighbors search using the "knn" search option. This allows you to query the vector space and retrieve the top matching documents based on vector proximity."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"GET /product_catalog/_search
{
  "knn": {
    "field": "product_vector",
    "query_vector": [0.13, 0.87, 0.46],
    "k": 2,
    "num_candidates": 10
  }
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Vector Search"},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure your query vector dimension matches the "dims" configuration defined in the index mapping."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Tune "num_candidates" carefully to balance search accuracy and query latency. Higher values increase recall at the expense of search speed."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use Elasticsearch Inference APIs to automatically generate embeddings from text fields using deployed NLP models."}]
